    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0735" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg655"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 541.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    telegram of the 11th instant, and confirm my telegram of the same date in
                    reply.</p>
                <p>The implied assumption expressed in your telegram that the Provisional Government
                    acted through its agencies at Gonaives in permitting the entry of French and
                    German vessels, is unsound, because that port and its approaches are held by
                    adverse forces.</p>
                <p>The argument is therefore illogical as well as irrelevant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
